{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280942-lunar-den-charms","id":280942,"title":"Lunar den charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-14T06:45:26-07:00","id":280942,"title":"Lunar den charms","content":"Ok, so I'm not that well versed in lunar charms - but IIRC there are lunar charms that allow you to conjure up a den of sorts that exists elsewhere - and then hide in it...<br /> <br /> 1) can you use it to hide stuff in it? Like, as an extra elsewhere storage charm<br /> <br /> 2) can you hide living things in it? Like, use it for kidnapping or hiding people you need to protect/extract (makes prison breaks easy)<br /> <br /> 3) if a lunar gets into the den, then can the den-opening be re-opened in other locations? Or can the lunar only exit where where he/she entered?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:04:19-07:00","id":280970,"title":"","content":"1) Yes, you can. It is a home for you in elsewhere. It doesn't vanish just because you close the door. Anything put in there remains.<br /> 2) Yes, you can. A Lunar player of mine has an amputated elder sidereal that he is holding for interrogation in his.<br /> 3) Once the Lunar enters the den the door closes and can only reopen where it was before. Now if the Lunar doesn't enter the den but instead piles people inside then shuts the door and moves to another location and reopens the door, yes. But once inside the lunar can only reopen the door to his hiding hole where it was before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:39:04-07:00","id":280995,"title":"","content":"Yes to everything, in an elder game I once made, one of the players took every available den-charms....and then used them to save a whole city population from a manse-5 blast after an epic fight within said manse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:01:04-07:00","id":281011,"title":"","content":"AFAIK there's nothing official that supports #3, but you could make an upgrade charm along the lines of allowing you to open the den to the last location of any of your forms. So if you have a sailor form that you last used in Skullstone, you could open the portal back to there.<br /> <br /> Or, for less book-keeping, just a &quot;once you've been there (or used a territory charm there, or whatever), you can open it to there&quot;. The thing is at this rate it's getting pretty close to Void-circle if it just lets you poof to anywhere in Creation. Transportation isn't really (read:at all) the purview of the den charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 10-14-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:09:51-07:00","id":281016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280942-lunar-den-charms?p=280995#post280995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes to everything, in an elder game I once made, one of the players took every available den-charms....and then used them to save a whole city population from a manse-5 blast after an epic fight within said manse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280942-lunar-den-charms?p=280970#post280970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Yes, you can. It is a home for you in elsewhere. It doesn't vanish just because you close the door. Anything put in there remains.<br /> 2) Yes, you can. A Lunar player of mine has an amputated elder sidereal that he is holding for interrogation in his.<br /> 3) Once the Lunar enters the den the door closes and can only reopen where it was before. Now if the Lunar doesn't enter the den but instead piles people inside then shuts the door and moves to another location and reopens the door, yes. But once inside the lunar can only reopen the door to his hiding hole where it was before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome and awesome<br /> <br /> This'll be quite useful for some... thing... I'm planning","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:22:08-07:00","id":281028,"title":"","content":"Huh never realized how much Lunar den Charms were basically Nagah Ananta or Bastet Den-Realms ported into Exalted. Not surprising though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:13:50-07:00","id":281107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280942-lunar-den-charms?p=281011#post281011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK there's nothing official that supports #3, but you could make an upgrade charm along the lines of allowing you to open the den to the last location of any of your forms. So if you have a sailor form that you last used in Skullstone, you could open the portal back to there.<br /> <br /> Or, for less book-keeping, just a &quot;once you've been there (or used a territory charm there, or whatever), you can open it to there&quot;. The thing is at this rate it's getting pretty close to Void-circle if it just lets you poof to anywhere in Creation. Transportation isn't really (read:at all) the purview of the den charm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Chancels are artifacts that can already do that. Perhaps you can use some territory charm and commit the motes so that in the future you can open the den to there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:25:37-07:00","id":281296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/280942-lunar-den-charms?p=281011#post281011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK there's nothing official that supports #3, but you could make an upgrade charm along the lines of allowing you to open the den to the last location of any of your forms. So if you have a sailor form that you last used in Skullstone, you could open the portal back to there.<br /> <br /> Or, for less book-keeping, just a &quot;once you've been there (or used a territory charm there, or whatever), you can open it to there&quot;. The thing is at this rate it's getting pretty close to Void-circle if it just lets you poof to anywhere in Creation. Transportation isn't really (read:at all) the purview of the den charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another option is the upgrade charm provides a certain number of doors(Essence -1, maybe?) to use in addition to the one you already have. These doors you can set down and &quot;tie&quot; to certain locations via either mote commitment or something else. You can enter through your personal door and that one remains connected to the place you left, but you can also leave through any of the &quot;tied&quot; doors.<br /> <br /> Tied doors also can be opened by anyone that knows the correct way of doing so(saying a certain key phrase, waiting for a certain time of day, etc), which you also have to use to open them. You can tell your allies how to open your doors so that you don't have to let them in yourself, but if your enemies find out how to open them, they can sneak into your den realm.<br /> <br /> To prevent easy travel all over Creation, you can set range limits on how far away your doors can be from each other.<br /> <br /> Or not, and Lunars can negotiate travel through their den realms with each other as their answer to the Sidereals using the Yu-Shan gates for travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:06:06-07:00","id":281398,"title":"","content":"I can see two options; either custom charms with lots of committed motes (alternatively, regular maintenance like that Wyld-Stabilising charm), or Sorcery.<br /> <br /> I can see territory/den charms that lets you exit your den in any territory you own. I can see gate-charms that lets you commit motes to create a stable, mystical entrance to your den which anyone might use, with the right knowledge or abilities. I can see den-pocket charms that lets you commit motes to create a stable pocket tied down to a specific location - and pocket-travel charms that lets you travel between your own pocket dimensions.<br /> <br /> I can also see Sorcery do pretty much all of the above, requiring a lot more time and effort to set up, but also not so draining in the long run. A spell that allows you to craft spirit-sanctum-esque pocket dimensions, tied down to specific locations - why not? A spell that lets you forge a stable pocket dimension in the middle of elsewhere - sure. A spell to travel to and from such dimensions - absolutely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}